From dfad3b0fb31c8de46e77de8f83c54c3c46765138 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:03:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app-item: Don't match system services to applications

The application ID taken from a process's systemd unit is meant for apps
started in a user session (see https://systemd.io/DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENTS/).
System services follow the same naming, so cupsd in cups.service was
listed as "Manage Printing" (cups.desktop, the CUPS web interface) with
a root tag, even with the launcher hidden through NoDisplay.

Only look at the unit for processes below /user.slice/; system services
fall back to the command line and are otherwise grouped under System.
---
 src/app-item.vala | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/app-item.vala b/src/app-item.vala
index db4c37e..f350a51 100644
--- a/src/app-item.vala
+++ b/src/app-item.vala
@@ -172,7 +172,11 @@ public class Usage.AppItem : Object {
             return appid_map[p.cmdline] ?? appid_map["system_waydroid"];
         }
 
-        if (cgroup != null) {
+        /* Only units of a user session can belong to an application: system
+         * services (e.g. cups.service for cupsd) would otherwise be matched to a
+         * launcher of the same name (cups.desktop, "Manage Printing"), including
+         * hidden ones, and listed as that application. */
+        if (cgroup != null && cgroup.has_prefix ("/user.slice/")) {
             /* Try to extract an application ID, this is a bit "magic".
              * See https://systemd.io/DESKTOP_ENVIRONMENTS/
              * and we also have some special cases for GNOME which is not
-- 
